    "args_note": "C throughout. The cut's ease (wide cut / fitted) after the dress research: the women's many-folded dress (IR-WOMEN, B for 'many-folded') 1.3; the knee-length tunics 1.15; the court robe 1.06 (its pleats are the reliefs' and baked in the mesh: drape.ts ROBE; more ease would undo them). Cloth: Blender's cloth settings for a medium wool or linen (vertex mass 0.2 kg, tension 15, shear 5, bending 0.5, the robe's stiffer 1.0, the dress's softer 0.3), collision 4 mm off the body, 60 frames at 24 fps (2.5 s: the drape settles), the gathered waist drawn in over the first 20. Groups' reference bodies: m03 (the outfits' reference), f02, c01. Arms are not colliders for skirts and upper garments (they swing in the game). Gathers: the waist of a gathered skirt is drawn in along a wave of 10 folds (the full-detail tube has 40 columns: 4 a fold) whose length is the wide cut's, so the cloth below buckles into folds; the court robe is not gathered (its pleats are baked)."
